From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:10:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kiln: the IFS error texts say slot

HelixScreen 1.2's wording for the Flashforge IFS errors
(flashforge_error_wording.cpp) says lane: "No filament in IFS lane 3",
"Filament stalled in IFS lane 2", "Check the lane's tube...". The AD5X
calls these positions slots, on its screen and in Kiln's docs, so the
texts now say slot: "No filament in IFS slot {1}", "Filament stalled in
IFS slot {1}", "Insert filament into slot {1}...", "...that slot's
tube...", and the toolhead runout texts likewise. English is the
identity locale (1.2 loads no en pack), so the source strings change;
the msgids in every catalog change with them, translations kept
(Turkish "yuva"). Test: the IFS error texts carry no "lane".

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
